---
import Section from './Section.astro';

// The agents the record has to answer for, and the question each one carries. They
// share a shape, which is the sentence under the table.
const agents = [
  { agent: 'Robot', question: 'which decision led to the failure, and who authorized it' },
  {
    agent: 'Drone',
    question: 'what the sensors saw before the link dropped, and whether the operator was warned',
  },
  {
    agent: 'Vehicle',
    question: 'which sensor and which model agreed before the intervention, and which did not',
  },
  { agent: 'Monitor', question: 'why the alarm fired, and which readings moved before it' },
  {
    agent: 'Pump',
    question:
      'how the dose and the response moved together over the last 24 hours, and whether the alarm was justified',
  },
  {
    agent: 'Sensor',
    question: 'how moisture and salinity moved after the last irrigation, and whether the budget was met',
  },
  { agent: 'Software agent', question: 'which model answered, at what cost, and on whose authority' },
];
---

<Section
  id="problem"
  label="Problem"
  title="The record cannot stay where it was made"
  lede="An edge device, a controller, or a sensor node produces a record of what it did and cannot run a database. Its own history is lost, or moved off the device to a system outside the operator’s control."
>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Agent</th>
          <th>The question it has to answer</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          agents.map((row) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="lead">{row.agent}</td>
              <td>{row.question}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Every question has the same shape: an origin, an event, and a time window, combined at once.
      The index a database answers with does not fit in the memory these agents have, so the
      workaround is to move the data off the device.
    </p>
    <p>
      This stayed contained while the actor was a person or a fixed program. The actor is a model
      now, and nothing binds the ask to the act.
    </p>
  </div>
</Section>
